A '''Movie Star''' (Japanese: '''スター''' ''Star'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] introduced in [[Pokémon Black and White Versions 2|Pokémon Black 2 and White 2]], appearing exclusively at [[Pokéstar Studios]]. They are [[Gym Leader]]s who act in movies.

There are two Movie Stars who appear in three different movie series.

[[Brycen]] appears as a Movie Star in both the [[Brycen-Man Series|Brycen-Man]] and [[Full Metal Cop Series]]. He plays the role of Masked Man {{DL|Pokéstar Studios characters|Brycen-Man}} in ''Brycen-Man - The Riolu Kid vs. Brycen Man'' (in {{ga|Nate}}'s version of the series), ''Brycen-Man - The Riolu Girl vs. Brycen Man'' (in {{ga|Rosa}}'s version of the series), ''Brycen-Man Strikes Back'', and ''Brycen-Man Strikes Back Harder''. He also plays the role of World Police {{DL|Pokéstar Studios characters|Mecha Cop}} in ''Full Metal Cop - Enter the Sneasel Ninja!'', ''Full Metal Cop 2 - The Sneasel Ninja's Trap'', and ''Full Metal Cop 4 - The Sneasel Ninja: The Final Case''. In the former series, he uses {{type|Dark}} Pokémon during filming. In the latter series, he uses {{t|Fighting}}- and {{type|Bug}} Pokémon.

Brycen is also the likeness for {{DL|Pokéstar Studios opponents|Brycen-Man|Prop H1}}, which plays the role of Brycen-Man in ''Brycen-Man Strikes Back 2''.

[[Sabrina]] appears as a Movie Star in the [[Mystery Doors of the Magical Land Series]]. She plays the roles of Strange Lady {{DL|Pokéstar Studios characters|???}} in ''Mystery Doors of the Magical Land - Beyond a Door'' and Magic Queen {{DL|Pokéstar Studios characters|Bellelba}} in ''Mystery Doors of the Magical Land 3 - Open a Door''. In the former, she uses {{type|Psychic}} Pokémon during filming. In the latter, she uses {{DL|Pokéstar Studios opponents|White Door|Props W1}} and {{DL|Pokéstar Studios opponents|Black Door|W2}}.

